WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.640
What if just one
lifestyle change

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.440
could help you
avoid getting cancer,

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.280
or diabetes,
or heart disease,

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.720
or high blood pressure?

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.000
This one change could cut
your risk of chronic disease

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.840
and add years to your life.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.600
Well, the simple solution to
so many of these problems

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.920
is to eat a healthy diet.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.280
In other words, one centered
around whole plant foods.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.880
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.080
I'm your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.320
Today I discuss the
safety and efficacy

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.920
of some unconventional
weight loss methods;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.400
everything from Botox and corsets
to siphons and tapeworms.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.720
A moderately obese person doing
moderately intense physical activity,

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.280
like biking or brisk walking, would burn
off approximately 350 calories an hour,

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.400
but most drinks, snacks,
and other processed junk

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.920
are consumed at a rate of
about 70 calories per minute.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.200
Therefore, it only takes five minutes
for someone to wipe out

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.720
a whole hour of exercise.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.120
Enter: the AspireAssist siphon assembly.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.600
It's a percutaneous gastrostomy device,
meaning surgeons cut a hole

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.560
in your stomach and tunnel a fistula
out through your abdominal wall,

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.120
so after each meal you can attach
a suctioning gadget to the hole

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.160
and directly drain out
your stomach contents.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:25.520
You could gorge on doughnuts,
spew them out through the hole

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.800
in your stomach, and then gorge
again on even more doughnuts.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.800
Have your cake, and eat it too...
and three, and four times.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.320
It's like bulimia without the aftertaste.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.000
Seems to be the quintessential
American invention, straight

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.800
from the land that brought you
Jell-O salads, spray cheese,

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:44.800
and deep-fried Snickers bars.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:49.840
Patients do lose weight, perhaps in
part because the fistula may interfere

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.800
with the relaxation of the
stomach wall during a meal.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.160
The process also requires drinking
lots of water and for food

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.120
to be chewed thoroughly, both
of which may help with weight loss

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.880
in other ways by increasing hydration
and slowing eating rate.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.960
Patients also started to make
healthier choices to avoid

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.480
unpleasant-appearing gastric
aspirate of unhealthy food choices.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.560
The tubing is clear and

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.080
evidently fried foods look particularly
gross as they're pumped out.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.680
All patients need to take supplemental
potassium, since it's sucked out

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.600
in the stomach juices; otherwise, they
risk becoming potassium deficient,

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:25.680
a common complication
in true bulimia,

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.040
but most side effects are just
minor wound complications.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.280
Serious adverse effects like
abdominal abscesses are rare.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.880
The big selling point is that the siphon
device does not alter the anatomy

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:42.480
of the gastrointestinal tract. Seems like
a low bar, but in today's Wild West

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.720
world of weight loss procedures,
you can't take anything for granted.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:50.320
Case in point: the
Duodenal-Jejunal Bypass Liner.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.120
Gastric bypass surgery works in part by
cutting out part of the small intestine

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.320
from the flow of food to help prevent
the absorption of calories.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:02.880
Instead of major surgery, how about
just dropping down a couple feet

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.760
of plastic tubing to line
the intestinal walls?

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:10.160
The problem with the EndoBarrier
is that it has to be anchored

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.240
in the digestive tract. This is
accomplished with 10 barbed hooks

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.920
that cause lacerations, accounting
for the majority of the 891 adverse

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.640
effects reported in 1,056 patients.
That's nearly 9 out of 10.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:28.000
Severe penetrating trauma,
resulting in esophageal perforation

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:28.960
or liver abscesses,

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:33.360
is thankfully more rare, occurring
in only about 1 in 27 patients.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.960
Concern has been raised about
the palatability of the AspireAssist

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:42.880
stomach pump, but the most
cringeworthy endoscopic procedure

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:47.120
I ran across in my research
was intestinal resurfacing.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:52.800
Why cover the inside of your intestines
with plastic to prevent absorption

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:58.000
when you can just thermally ablate
the superficial duodenal mucosa?

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:04.160
In other words, have your intestinal
lining burned off, or rather, resurfaced.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:09.520
Surgeons have tried injecting botox into
the stomach walls of obese individuals,

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:12.800
hoping it would partially
paralyze their gastric muscles,

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:16.240
slow stomach emptying, make people
feel fuller longer, and lose weight.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.880
It didn't work.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:23.440
Researchers in Sweden tried
randomizing people to wear corsets

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:26.880
for 12 to 16 hours a day, seven
days a week, for nine months.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:30.560
And it didn't work.
You can guess why.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.360
The study subjects
just didn't wear them.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.360
The corset was perceived
as uncomfortable. Duh!

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.160
Sanitized tapeworms have
evidently been widely advertised

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.680
as a weight loss remedy since
back in the early 1900s.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.840
The fact that living tapeworms
have been discovered

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.680
during bariatric surgery operations
suggests infesting yourself

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:56.320
with parasites may not
be particularly effective either.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:00.720
Speaking of disgusting strategies,
how about disgust itself?

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:05.280
A study entitled "Harnessing the power
of disgust: a randomized trial to reduce

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.280
high-calorie food appeal through
implicit priming" tried using

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.160
subliminal messages
to ruin people's appetite.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.160
Immediately before images of healthy
foods, researchers showed people

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.640
happy images like a group of kittens
in a 20-millisecond flash.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.880
That's too quick to
consciously register,

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:26.160
but the hope was to plant
a positive imprint on the brain.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:29.680
Before images of high-calorie
foods like ice cream though,

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.680
they instead flashed scenes
of a cockroach on a slice of pizza,

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.040
vomit in an unclean lavatory,
a burn wound...

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.600
Apparently, it worked!

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:42.560
Subjects subsequently
reported a reduced desire

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:46.000
to eat high-calorie foods,
though this wasn't tested directly.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:51.760
The researchers conclude subliminal
revulsion may be a successful tactic

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:56.560
to combat the onslaught of food
cues that promote unhealthy eating.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:02.080
The rest of the world look on
bemused by American machinations,

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.360
penning commentaries like

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.560
"A View From Across the Pond...
Don't Let Them Eat Cake!"

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:12.960
A paper in the journal Obesity Surgery
entitled "What are the Yanks Doing?"

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:17.280
reviewed the U.S. experience with
Implantable Gastric Stimulation,

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.800
inserting electrodes into the
muscular layer of the stomach wall.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:25.760
When that didn't work, we tried
Colon Electrical Stimulation.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:28.880
Even more shocking
were studies like

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:34.240
"Repetitive electric brain stimulation
reduces food intake in humans."

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.800
Though placing deep brain
electrodes is considered a

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:40.800
complication-prone operation,
scientists have long pondered

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:45.200
whether placing an electrode somewhere
in the brain could make people eat less.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:49.680
Holes were drilled through the
skulls of five obese individuals,

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:54.480
and wires were pushed into their brains
for electro-stimulatory exploration.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:58.960
Once they poked around and found spots
where they were able to elicit convincing

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:04.880
hunger responses, they sent enough juice
in to fry out electro-coagulatory lesions.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:09.600
It seemed to work in cats and monkeys,
but the researchers found that burning

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:13.920
holes in people's brains did not
produce weight loss in obese humans.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:18.800
Thankfully, as I aim to explain
in my book, How Not to Diet,

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.920
healthy sustainable weight loss
isn't brain surgery.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.400
In our next story, we look
at how sham surgery trials

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:31.750
have shown us that some of our most
popular surgeries are themselves shams.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:37.120
Intragastric balloons arrived
with much fanfare in the 1980s,

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:40.320
balloons that could be
implanted into the stomach

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:43.040
and inflated with air or water
to fill up much of the space.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:47.680
Sadly, surgical devices are often brought
to the market before there is adequate

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:52.000
evidence of safety and effectiveness,
and the balloons were no exception.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:56.480
The Gastric Bubble had its bubble burst
when a study at the Mayo Clinic found

00:07:56.480 --> 00:08:01.280
that 8 out of 10 balloons spontaneously
deflated, which is potentially dangerous

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:04.240
as they could pass into the intestines
and cause an obstruction,

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:07.840
but not before causing gastric
erosions in half the patients,

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.280
damaging the stomach lining.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:13.680
The kicker is that in terms of inducing
weight loss, it didn't even work.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:18.960
Eventually, it was pulled from the
market, but now balloons are back.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:25.360
After a 33-year hiatus, the FDA started
approving a whole slew of intragastric

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:29.920
balloons in 2015, immediately resulting
in more than 5,000 placements.

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:34.880
By then the Sunshine Act had passed,
which forced drug companies

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:38.320
and the surgical and medical device
industry to disclose any payments

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:41.600
they were making to physicians
to shine a disinfecting light

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:45.440
on industry enticements.
By now most people know about

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:50.000
the overly cozy financial relationship
doctors can have with Big Pharma,

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:54.160
but fewer may realize that
surgeons can also get payments

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:56.080
from companies for
the devices they use.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:01.280
The 100 top recipients of industry
payments received an unbelievable

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:05.040
$12 million from device
companies in a single year.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:08.560
Yet outrageously, when
they published papers,

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:12.320
only a minority disclosed
the blatant conflict of interest.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:16.400
The benefit of balloons over
most types of bariatric surgery

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:19.760
is that they're reversible, but
that doesn't mean they're benign.

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:22.080
The FDA has released
a series of advisories

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.720
about the risks that
include patient deaths.

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:29.120
Wait. How could someone
suffer a stomach perforation

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:35.040
with a smooth rounded object? By
causing the patient to puke so much

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:38.880
they rupture their stomach
and die, that's how.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:44.160
Nausea and vomiting are unsurprisingly
very common side effects,

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:48.240
affecting the majority of those who
have balloons placed inside them.

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:51.120
Persistent vomiting likely
also explains cases of

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:54.720
life-threatening nutrient deficiencies
after balloon implantation.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.680
Some complications,
such as bowel obstruction,

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:01.520
are due to the balloon deflating, but
others, oddly enough, are due to

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:03.840
the balloons suddenly overinflating,

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:08.160
causing pain, vomiting, abdominal
distention. This was first noticed

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:11.840
in breast implants, as
documented in reports such as

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:16.240
"The Phenomenon of the Spontaneously
Autoinflating Breast Implant."

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:19.440
Out of nowhere, the
implants just start growing,

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:21.760
increasing breast volume by
an average of more than 50%.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.400
"It remains," one review noted,

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:27.200
"an underreported and poorly
understood phenomenon."

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.880
Interestingly, breast implants
were actually used as some

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:33.680
of the first failed experimental
intragastric balloons.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:38.320
As with any medical decision, though,
it's all about risks versus benefits.

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:42.400
Industry-funded trials display notable
weight loss, but it's hard to tease out

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:46.000
the effect of the balloon alone from
the accompanying supervised diet

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.360
and lifestyle changes prescribed
along with them in the studies.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:53.200
In drug trials, you can randomize
subjects to sugar pills,

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:57.440
but how do you eliminate the placebo
effect of undergoing a procedure?

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:00.960
Perform sham surgery.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.800
In 2002, a courageous study was published
in the New England Journal of Medicine.

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:11.520
The most common orthopedic surgery,
arthroscopic surgery of the knee, was

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:16.000
put to the test. Billions of dollars are
spent sticking scopes into knee joints

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:19.120
and cutting away damaged tissue
in osteoarthritis and knee injuries,

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:20.960
but does it actually work?

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:25.600
Knee pain sufferers were randomized
to get the actual surgery versus

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:30.240
a sham surgery in which they
actually sliced into people's knees

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:34.320
and pretended to perform the procedure,
complete with splashing saline,

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:36.800
but never actually did
anything within the joint.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.080
The trial caused an uproar.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:43.920
How could you randomize people
to get cut open for fake surgery?

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:47.440
Professional medical associations
questioned the ethics of the surgeons

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:51.200
as well as the sanity of the patients
who agreed to be part of the trial.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:54.720
But guess what happened?

00:11:55.520 --> 00:12:01.040
Sure, the surgical patients got better,
but so did the placebo patients.

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:03.680
The surgeries had no actual effect.

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:10.000
Currently, rotator cuff shoulder surgery
is facing the same crisis of confidence.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:14.720
When intragastric balloons were put
to the test, sham-controlled trials show

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:19.520
both older and newer devices sometimes
fail to offer any weight loss benefit.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:23.760
Even when they do work, the weight loss
may be temporary because balloons

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:26.560
are only allowed to stay in
for 6 months, at which point

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:29.200
the deflation risk gets too great.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:31.680
Why can't you just keep
putting new ones in?

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:35.600
That's been tried and failed to
improve long-term weight outcomes.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:38.480
A sham-controlled trial showed
that any effects of the balloon

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:41.280
on appetite and satiety
may vanish with time,

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.920
perhaps as your body gets
used to the new normal.

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:47.760
What sham surgery trials
have shown us is that some of

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.720
our most popular surgeries
are themselves shams.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:55.120
Doctors like to pride themselves on
being men and women of science.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:58.640
We rightly rail, for example, against
the antivaccination movement.

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:02.160
Many of us in medicine have been
troubled by the political trend

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:04.080
of people choosing their own facts.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:09.120
But when I read that some of these still-
popular surgeries are not only useless

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:12.240
but may actually make things worse
— for example, increasing the risk

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:14.560
of progression to a total
knee replacement —

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:17.200
I can't help but think
we are hardly immune

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:20.720
to our own versions of fake
news and alternative facts.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:25.840
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:29.120
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:32.880
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:37.200
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:42.320
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:45.600
please go to the Nutrition Facts Podcast
landing page.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.040
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:52.240
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite to each of these topics.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:57.120
My latest two books are
“How to Survive a Pandemic”,

00:13:57.760 --> 00:14:00.880
available on e-book, audiobook,
or actual book.

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:04.960
And the “How Not to Diet Cookbook”,
with more than 100 recipes for

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:07.120
delicious and nutritious meals.

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:12.560
All the proceeds I receive from
the sales of my books go to charity.

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:17.200
NutritionFacts.org is a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:19.040
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:23.200
on the latest in nutrition research
via bite-sized videos and articles.

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:25.040
Everything on the website is free.

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:28.080
There’s no ads, no corporate sponsorship.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:31.600
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:34.960
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:37.920
as a tribute to my grandmother,

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:43.840
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

